Feature: Compound Drug Screening Analysis and Aggregation

  This feature performs compound screening analysis on the purgo_playground.compound_drug_analysis table, including filtering, aggregation, joining, scoring, and categorization to generate comprehensive insights per therapeutic area.

  Background:
    Given the source table is "purgo_playground.compound_drug_analysis" in Unity Catalog "purgo_databricks"
    And the table contains columns: study_id, compound_id, mutation_id, therapeutic_area, drug_name, ic50, auc, efficacy, toxicity, potency, sample_size, mutation_frequency, mutation_severity, compound_concentration, cell_viability, growth_inhibition, result, approved_flag, validation_status, status, created_by, score1, score2, score3, score4, score5

  # Happy Path: Filtering, Aggregation, Join, Scoring, Categorization

  Scenario: Filter and aggregate compound drug analysis data by therapeutic area
    Given the compound_drug_analysis table contains valid data
    When the data is filtered to include only rows where approved_flag = 1 and validation_status = "valid"
    And the filtered data is grouped by therapeutic_area
    Then calculate the following per therapeutic_area:
      | Metric                | Calculation                                      |
      | avg_ic50              | Average of ic50, ignoring nulls                  |
      | avg_auc               | Average of auc, ignoring nulls                   |
      | avg_efficacy          | Average of efficacy, ignoring nulls              |
      | total_sample_size     | Sum of sample_size, treating null as 0           |
      | study_count           | Count of unique study_id                         |
    And the aggregated results are joined with the filtered data on therapeutic_area
    And for each row, overall_score is calculated as the average of score1, score2, score3, score4, score5, ignoring nulls
    And potential_category is assigned as follows:
      | overall_score range | potential_category    |
      | 70 <= score <= 100 | High Potential        |
      | 60 <= score < 70   | Moderate Potential    |
      | score < 60         | Low Potential         |
    And the final output includes all source columns, aggregated metrics, overall_score, and potential_category

  # Error Scenarios

  Scenario Outline: Error when required columns are missing
    Given the compound_drug_analysis table is missing column "<missing_column>"
    When the analysis is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Column <missing_column> not found in source table"

    Examples:
      | missing_column   |
      | ic50            |
      | auc             |
      | efficacy        |
      | sample_size     |
      | study_id        |
      | score1          |
      | score2          |
      | score3          |
      | score4          |
      | score5          |
      | therapeutic_area|

  Scenario: Error when no rows match filter criteria
    Given the compound_drug_analysis table contains no rows where approved_flag = 1 and validation_status = "valid"
    When the analysis is executed
    Then the output is an empty result set

  Scenario Outline: Error when data types are invalid
    Given the compound_drug_analysis table contains a row where <column> has an invalid value "<invalid_value>"
    When the analysis is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Invalid value '<invalid_value>' in column <column>"

    Examples:
      | column      | invalid_value |
      | ic50        | "abc"         |
      | auc         | "NaN"         |
      | efficacy    | "null"        |
      | sample_size | "-10"         |
      | score1      | "xyz"         |

  # Data-driven Scenarios for Scoring and Categorization

  Scenario Outline: Calculate overall_score and potential_category for various score combinations
    Given a compound_drug_analysis row with score1=<score1>, score2=<score2>, score3=<score3>, score4=<score4>, score5=<score5>
    When overall_score is calculated as the average of non-null scores
    Then the overall_score is <expected_score>
    And the potential_category is <expected_category>

    Examples:
      | score1 | score2 | score3 | score4 | score5 | expected_score | expected_category   |
      | 80     | 90     | 85     | 75     | 95     | 85             | High Potential      |
      | 65     | 62     | 68     | 70     | 66     | 66.2           | Moderate Potential  |
      | 55     | 58     | 59     | 57     | 56     | 57             | Low Potential       |
      | 100    | null   | 90     | 80     | 70     | 85             | High Potential      |
      | null   | null   | 60     | 65     | 70     | 65             | Moderate Potential  |
      | null   | null   | null   | null   | null   | null           | Low Potential       |

  # Null and Missing Value Handling

  Scenario Outline: Null handling in aggregation and scoring
    Given a compound_drug_analysis row with ic50=<ic50>, auc=<auc>, efficacy=<efficacy>, sample_size=<sample_size>, score1=<score1>, score2=<score2>, score3=<score3>, score4=<score4>, score5=<score5>
    When aggregation and scoring are performed
    Then null values in ic50, auc, efficacy are ignored in averages
    And null sample_size is treated as 0 in total_sample_size
    And overall_score is calculated as the average of non-null scores
    And if all scores are null, overall_score is null and potential_category is "Low Potential"

    Examples:
      | ic50  | auc   | efficacy | sample_size | score1 | score2 | score3 | score4 | score5 |
      | 50.0  | null  | 80.0     | 10          | 80     | 90     | null   | 85     | 95     |
      | null  | null  | null     | null        | null   | null   | null   | null   | null   |
      | 60.0  | 70.0  | null     | 5           | 65     | 62     | 68     | 70     | 66     |

  # Output Format

  Scenario: Output includes all required columns and derived metrics
    Given the analysis is completed successfully
    When the results are displayed
    Then the output includes:
      | Column Name           | Description                                      |
      | study_id              | Source study identifier                          |
      | compound_id           | Source compound identifier                       |
      | mutation_id           | Source mutation identifier                       |
      | therapeutic_area      | Source therapeutic area                          |
      | drug_name             | Source drug name                                 |
      | ic50                  | Source ic50 value                                |
      | auc                   | Source auc value                                 |
      | efficacy              | Source efficacy value                            |
      | toxicity              | Source toxicity value                            |
      | potency               | Source potency value                             |
      | sample_size           | Source sample size                               |
      | mutation_frequency    | Source mutation frequency                        |
      | mutation_severity     | Source mutation severity                         |
      | compound_concentration| Source compound concentration                    |
      | cell_viability        | Source cell viability                            |
      | growth_inhibition     | Source growth inhibition                         |
      | result                | Source result                                    |
      | approved_flag         | Source approved flag                             |
      | validation_status     | Source validation status                         |
      | status                | Source status                                    |
      | created_by            | Source created by                                |
      | score1                | Source score1                                    |
      | score2                | Source score2                                    |
      | score3                | Source score3                                    |
      | score4                | Source score4                                    |
      | score5                | Source score5                                    |
      | avg_ic50              | Aggregated average ic50 per therapeutic_area     |
      | avg_auc               | Aggregated average auc per therapeutic_area      |
      | avg_efficacy          | Aggregated average efficacy per therapeutic_area |
      | total_sample_size     | Aggregated total sample_size per therapeutic_area|
      | study_count           | Aggregated count of unique study_id per area     |
      | overall_score         | Calculated average of scores per row             |
      | potential_category    | Categorized potential per row                    |

  # Join Analysis

  Scenario: Join filtered data with aggregated metrics on therapeutic_area
    Given filtered compound_drug_analysis data and aggregated metrics per therapeutic_area
    When the join is performed on therapeutic_area
    Then each row in the output contains both the original row data and the corresponding aggregated metrics for its therapeutic_area

  # Data Scope

  Scenario: Analysis is performed on the entire compound_drug_analysis table
    Given no additional filtering criteria are specified
    When the analysis is executed
    Then all rows in compound_drug_analysis are considered for filtering, aggregation, and output

  # Business Logic for Study Count

  Scenario: Study count is calculated as count of unique study_id per therapeutic_area
    Given the data is grouped by therapeutic_area
    When study_count is calculated
    Then study_count equals the number of distinct study_id values in each therapeutic_area group

  # Mapping/Enrichment

  Scenario: No mapping or enrichment from other tables is performed
    Given the requirements do not specify enrichment from therapeutic_area_mapping or other tables
    When the analysis is executed
    Then only data from compound_drug_analysis is used

  # Versioning/Automation

  Scenario: No versioning or update frequency requirements specified
    Given the requirements do not specify automation or scheduling
    When the analysis is executed
    Then the process is assumed to be ad-hoc and manual

